# Requirement Analysis Phase

## Project Title: ComicCraft – AI Comic Story Creator Using Gemini Models

### 1. Introduction

The requirement analysis phase identifies the functional and non-functional requirements of the ComicCraft application.

ComicCraft is an AI-powered application that uses Google Gemini models to generate comic stories, characters, dialogues, and scene descriptions from user-provided prompts. It aims to simplify comic creation through an interactive and user-friendly platform.

### 2. Functional Requirements

Functional requirements describe the features and operations of the system.

| S.No. | Requirement         | Description                                                                       |
| ----- | ------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| 1     | User Input          | Users can enter their own story ideas or prompts.                                 |
| 2     | Story Generation    | Gemini generates creative comic stories based on user input.                      |
| 3     | Genre Selection     | Users can select genres such as comedy, horror, fantasy, and adventure.           |
| 4     | Character Creation  | The system generates character names, personalities, and descriptions.            |
| 5     | Panel Generation    | The story is divided into multiple comic panels.                                  |
| 6     | Dialogue Generation | The system generates dialogues for each panel.                                    |
| 7     | AI Image Generation | The system creates comic illustrations using a compatible image-generation model. |
| 8     | Story Editing       | Users can edit and regenerate the generated story.                                |
| 9     | Comic Preview       | Users can view the generated comic panels.                                        |
| 10    | Comic Export        | Users can save or download the completed comic.                                   |

### 3. Non-Functional Requirements

Non-functional requirements define the quality and performance of the application.

| S.No. | Requirement     | Description                                                     |
| ----- | --------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------- |
| 1     | Usability       | The interface should be simple and user-friendly.               |
| 2     | Performance     | The system should generate content within a reasonable time.    |
| 3     | Reliability     | The application should handle errors and API failures properly. |
| 4     | Security        | User data and API keys must be protected.                       |
| 5     | Scalability     | The system should support an increasing number of users.        |
| 6     | Compatibility   | The application should work on different browsers and devices.  |
| 7     | Maintainability | The application should be easy to update and maintain.          |

