### 6. User Requirements

The ComicCraft application should allow users to:

* Enter a creative story prompt.
* Select a preferred comic genre.
* Generate stories using Gemini models.
* Create characters and dialogues.
* Generate and preview comic panels.
* Edit and customize the generated content.
* Save or download the final comic.

### 7. Feasibility Analysis

| Feasibility             | Description                                                                                                  |
| ----------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |
| Technical Feasibility   | Gemini API and web technologies can support AI-based comic story generation.                                 |
| Economic Feasibility    | The project can use free or low-cost development tools, depending on API usage and hosting costs.            |
| Operational Feasibility | The simple interface makes the application easy for beginners to use.                                        |
| Schedule Feasibility    | The project can be developed in stages, starting with story generation and then adding comic panel features. |

### 8. Expected Outcome

The requirement analysis phase defines the essential features, technical needs, and quality standards of ComicCraft.

The expected outcome is an AI-powered comic story creator that transforms user ideas into structured comic stories with characters, dialogues, and panels using Google Gemini models. The system aims to reduce manual effort, encourage creativity, and provide an easy comic creation experience.

